caption: General Mastery Benefits
tradition-component: general-mastery-benefits

Each of the two original Revelator Powers gains ordinary Advanced purchase access to its single-branch abilities. Existing Basic constructions remain as purchased until rebuilt and paid for normally.

Conjunction Abilities built from the two original Revelator Powers gain Master Psi access. Unless Whole Truth changes the cap calculation, use the lower of the two Revelator Talent levels as Conjunction Rating.

While expressing a Revelation, Wild Branch Manifestation may use Wild Ability to temporarily manifest a legal Master-access Psi ability belonging solely to either original Revelator Power, subject to normal Wild Ability limits.

Any non-Talent ability purchased through Revelator may replace Psionic, -10%, plus Super, -10%, with Eldritch, -5%, paying the normal character-point difference. Future Revelator abilities may be purchased with Eldritch, -5% directly.

The chosen Path gains its Origin-facing Mastery expansion described in the Path section.

The two original Revelator Talents remain fixed. Mastery does not itself grant another Talent, unrestricted access to another Power, Universal Talent, Expanded Core, or free character points. Additional Psi or Super Talents interact with Revelator only where the mastered Path explicitly permits it.
